cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "open-ml-notebooks: original, executed experiments across machine learning, deep learning, and reinforcement learning"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lounissi
    given-names: Elyes
    email: pilot.tun@gmail.com
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/ELounissi/open-ml-notebooks"
url: "https://github.com/ELounissi/open-ml-notebooks"
abstract: >-
  A collection of self-contained Jupyter notebooks, each posing one falsifiable
  question about a machine learning method and answering it on an openly
  licensed dataset. Covers supervised, unsupervised, and self-supervised
  learning, deep learning, generative models, graph learning, and reinforcement
  learning. Every notebook ships executed, with figures that were read before
  they were published.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - deep learning
  - reinforcement learning
  - self-supervised learning
  - jupyter notebooks
  - open datasets
  - reproducible research
  - data science education
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-08-06
